{"timestamp": "2026-02-04 20:17:23.450384", "event": "llm_start", "messages": "content='Based on the diagnosis report: ### Troubleshooting Diagnosis Report\\n\\n#### Network Description\\nThe network is an SDN star topology with one central switch (switch_0) and multiple edge switches (switch_1, switch_2, switch_3, switch_4). Hosts (host_1, host_2, host_3, host_4) are connected to edge switches, and all devices share a single access subnet (10.0.0.0/24). The SDN controller operates at 20.0.0.100 and manages the switches via OpenFlow.\\n\\n#### Reachability Test Results\\nPing tests were conducted between hosts to assess connectivity and network health. Below are the results:\\n\\n1. **Host-to-Host Connectivity**\\n   - **host_1 → host_3**: \\n     - Packets transmitted: 2, Packets received: 2\\n     - Loss: 0%\\n     - Average RTT: 16.656 ms\\n     - Status: OK\\n   - **host_1 → host_2**: \\n     - Packets transmitted: 2, Packets received: 2\\n     - Loss: 0%\\n     - Average RTT: 10.023 ms\\n     - Status: OK\\n   - **host_2 → host_3**: \\n     - Packets transmitted: 2, Packets received: 2\\n     - Loss: 0%\\n     - Average RTT: 15.826 ms\\n     - Status: OK\\n   - **host_3 → host_2**: \\n     - Packets transmitted: 2, Packets received: 2\\n     - Loss: 0%\\n     - Average RTT: 12.412 ms\\n     - Status: OK\\n   - **host_4 → host_3**: \\n     - Packets transmitted: 2, Packets received: 2\\n     - Loss: 0%\\n     - Average RTT: 17.144 ms\\n     - Status: OK\\n   - **host_4 → host_2**: \\n     - Packets transmitted: 2, Packets received: 2\\n     - Loss: 0%\\n     - Average RTT: 15.898 ms\\n     - Status: OK\\n\\n#### Observations\\n1. **Connectivity**: All hosts successfully communicated with each other, with no packet loss observed in any of the tests. This indicates that the basic connectivity between hosts is functional.\\n2. **Latency**: The average round-trip times (RTTs) are within acceptable ranges for a local network. However, there is some variability in RTTs, with maximum RTTs occasionally spiking (e.g., host_4 → host_3: max RTT = 32.948 ms). This could indicate transient network delays or congestion.\\n3. **Status**: All tests returned an \"OK\" status, confirming that the network paths between hosts are operational.\\n\\n#### Next Steps\\nWhile the reachability tests show no immediate connectivity issues, further investigation may be warranted to:\\n- Analyze the SDN controller\\'s configuration and logs to ensure proper flow rules are installed.\\n- Examine switch performance and OpenFlow communication to detect any anomalies.\\n- Investigate potential causes of RTT variability, such as network congestion or hardware limitations.\\n\\nThis report provides a preliminary assessment of the network\\'s health based on host-to-host connectivity tests. Further diagnostics may be required to ensure optimal performance and stability., please provide the submission. Do not submit if no report available.' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={} id='1907e64b-e2f9-4069-8601-a9f548e51083'", "model": {"lc": 1, "type": "constructor", "id": ["langchain", "chat_models", "openai", "ChatOpenAI"], "kwargs": {"model_name": "kt-gpt-oss-rh014", "temperature": 0.0, "openai_api_key": {"lc": 1, "type": "secret", "id": ["OPENAI_API_KEY"]}, "openai_api_base": "https://dev.kora.kt.co.kr/v2", "request_timeout": 180.0, "max_retries": 2}, "name": "ChatOpenAI"}}
